; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   926  /* SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   927     \ID SBSW_DET_1    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   928       \DESCRIPTION Array Write Access (P6 - Wrong Initialization and Usage of a Pointer due to Wrong Index)
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   929        Update of log buffer in Det_LogError. Due to the code structure the calculated array index cannot exceed the array size. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   930        Therefore this is not critical and no out of bounds array access can occur. The index is unconditionally reset to zero if is equal or greater than DET_LOGBUFFERSIZE.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   931       \COUNTERMEASURE \N The code structure already ensures that the index cannot exceed the size of the array.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   932     \ID SBSW_DET_2    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   933       \DESCRIPTION Array Write Access (P6 - Wrong Initialization and Usage of a Pointer due to Wrong Index)
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   934        Initialization of global array in Det_Init. Both the array size and the loop is is controlled by generated #defines DET_*SIZE. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   935        Therefore this is not critical and no out of bounds array access can occur.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   936       \COUNTERMEASURE \N The code structure already ensures that the index cannot exceed the size of the array.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   937     \ID SBSW_DET_3    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   938       \DESCRIPTION Function Call
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   939        Calls to CANoe API or C stdlib with pointer parameters. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   940        This code is only active in case of the CANoe emulation or vtt environment which is not used production code.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   941       \COUNTERMEASURE \N This code part is not active for embedded production targets.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   942     \ID SBSW_DET_4    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   943       \DESCRIPTION Function Pointer Call
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   944        Iteration over generated function pointer tables using identifiers generated by the ComStackLib. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   945       \COUNTERMEASURE \N Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib assures correct dimension of arrays and consistency of corresponding size definitions.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   946        The validity of the callout function names is covered by SMI-5.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   947     \ID SBSW_DET_6    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   948       \DESCRIPTION Function Call
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   949        call of internal functions Det_CheckFilterMatch and Det_LogError (both functions cannot be called by the application or other modules)
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   950        There could be a Null pointer dereferencing if these functions are called with invalid pointer parameters.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   951        However, at the three places in Det_ReportError where these functions are called the calls always uses valid pointers.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   952        So there is no need for an additional Null pointer check in these functions.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   953       \COUNTERMEASURE \N The code structure already ensures that the functions are always called with valid pointers.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   954     \ID SBSW_DET_7    
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   955       \DESCRIPTION Pointer Write Access (P1 - Wrong Pointer Parameter)
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   956        The function Det_GetVersionInfo writes to the object referenced by parameter versioninfo. The structure is provided by application code and passed to the DET. 
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   957        The fault pattern P9 is already prevented by a NULL pointer check.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   958       \COUNTERMEASURE \N The caller ensures that the pointers passed to the parameter versioninfo is valid.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\Det\Det.c	   959     \ID SBSW_DET_8    
